## Checks and completion

Select outcome-focused checks for changed behavior: existing relevant unit and
integration tests, practical regression coverage, and official parsers/loaders
for configuration. Prompt instructions receive content review and scenario
walkthroughs, not literal phrase tests or executable prompt-policy replicas.
Keep effective-tool/runtime checks when exposure changes. No mandatory TDD or
RED/GREEN transcript, new validation framework, validation manifest, or unrelated
application suite merely to finish. Repair or escalate known failed required
checks and defects; report what was actually checked and its limits.

Commit intended work on the approved effort branch, never main. Honor upfront
Git disposition: when mergeback is approved, integrate locally after successful
required checks/reviews, then clean only effort-owned worktrees after preserving
intended work and confirming it is reachable. Substantive conflicts or unresolved
blockers require escalation. Leave-unmerged keeps the committed branch; branch
deletion is not implied. No push without explicit authority. Preserve unrelated
changes and unknown worktrees. Use `finishing-a-development-branch` where useful,
without a new finalize-before/after-human-checks question.

Manual checks do not block mergeback, effort-owned cleanup or goal completion.
After required finalization succeeds, complete the active saved goal, if any,
before the all-done summary. Do not block a goal merely to await manual checks.
Report completed work, actual checks, remaining risks/manual steps and pending
Jira sync. Source changes, installed copies and runtime reload are separate facts.
